 ### Graph-Based Oblique Slice Generation
-A method to efficiently generate a stack of oblique slices orthogonal to the viewing direction by treating each slice as a 2D 'scanplane' and exploiting scanplane coherence, avoiding polygon clipping [S2]. It differs from the brute-force approach (calculate plane equation, generate large triangle, clip to data set, generate texture coordinates) by generating slices directly with no clipping, avoiding precision problems and artifacts from numeric imprecision in clipping [S2]. It is chosen when oblique slices are required and efficiency is a concern [S2].
+A method to efficiently generate a stack of oblique slices orthogonal to the viewing direction by treating each slice as a 2D 'scanplane' and exploiting scanplane coherence, avoiding polygon clipping [S2]. It differs from the brute-force approach (calculate plane equation, generate large triangle, clip to data set, generate texture coordinates) by generating slices directly with no clipping, avoiding precision problems and artifacts from numeric imprecision in clipping [S2]. It is chosen when oblique slices are required and efficiency is a concern [S2]. See also [Polygon-based Volumetric Rendering with Depth Peeling](8389-polygon-based-volumetric-rendering-with-depth-peeling.md), [Object Aligned Planes Volume Rendering](11411-object-aligned-planes-volume-rendering.md), and [3D Texture Slicing with Back-to-Front Blending](12611-3d-texture-slicing-with-back-to-front-blending.md).
 
